{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "עיניכם רואות", :translit "eineichem ro'ot", :gloss "your eyes see"} {:he "והראיתי לכם", :translit "ve'he'reiti lachem", :gloss "and I showed you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "עיניכם רואות", :b "והראיתי לכם"}], :frame {:text "Joseph tells his brothers 'your eyes see' that it is his mouth speaking (Genesis 45:12). The Ba'al HaTurim reads this as the brothers seeing Joseph's face directly, without an interpreter between them.", :sources ["Genesis 45:12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כי פי המדבר אליכם", :translit "ki pi ha'medaber aleichem", :gloss "for my mouth speaking to you"} {:he "בעגלה ערופה", :translit "be'eglah arufah", :gloss "with a slain calf"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כי פי המדבר אליכם", :b "בעגלה ערופה"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'ki pi ha'medaber aleichem' signals that Jacob had transmitted to Joseph a sign involving 'eglah arufah' — the rite described in Deuteronomy 21:1–9 in which a heifer is slain at a wadi when an unknown murderer is sought. The Ba'al HaTurim alludes to a tradition that Jacob gave Joseph a distinctive teaching or sign tied to this rite as a marker of authentic transmission.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 21:1-9" "Genesis 45:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "עיניכם רואות", :a-value 813, :b "והראיתי לכם", :b-value 722, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:a-value 472, :b-value 471, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "בעגלה ערופה", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "כי פי המדבר אליכם"}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:41.141551401Z", :model "glm-5.2"}